dressed Sumantra, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-39-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2034009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7bff91fde0157218c15f376622c64ebf47ccd43a5fe81c7db287142db8b4a15a","compact":"dfe1ee35ca5749b96cbe60317ee3d3d8753002faf1123ab9a0fd9f811f8c1842","nasal":"da0f13ed85ac693c456069c423cd3b0d0f4e3f1b5b942095d62e3e768169ae20"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-34-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":34,"verse":10,"english":"Yoking a riding car with excellent horses, do you come hither; and take the exalted one to the south of the kingdom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-39-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2034010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f8dd796d5c55d11393ba5830bd08891a8b4f11c901707cae353d56fdc70ba60d","compact":"aeceac27b39a7ee1676fa8508ec771f4a04cc5ceb89b8001fc504e0c2b351918","nasal":"aeceac27b39a7ee1676fa8508ec771f4a04cc5ceb89b8001fc504e0c2b351918"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-34-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":34,"verse":11,"english":"The virtuous and heroic Rāma is being banished by his father and, mother Even this methinks will be asserted as the fruit of the virtues possessed by the pious.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-39-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2034011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c864eafb58b8287b69f13653fb39ef6d04112f6b1a5d17fa5cf7a0ab952fd8d","compact":"27d5ac5e9410e22919d0ac1468faaf206c601dcfa28948a3a5058395bb62db26","nasal":"27d5ac5e9410e22919d0ac1468faaf206c601dcfa28948a3a5058395bb62db26"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-34-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":34,"verse":12,"english":"Receiving the mandate of the sovereign, Sumantra endued with fleet vigour, yoking a car adorned with horses, came there.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-39-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2034012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"47de006aab7892c9b7456a0cca23dfa0114103b9408810c78414deea24d6cda8","compact":"d9a3813cb9821142cc0edd1617cd55b94a899565ae51c61fe9f5de990acb1494","nasal":"d30970c500c34b61b42650fad7987adf202dd3927d248b65d6ad230b5e382f59"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-34-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":34,"verse":13,"english":"Then the charioteer with joined hands announced to the prince that the car adorned with gold was ready, yoked with excellent horses.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-39-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2034013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6dbfa29a12a1058dd37c1dd3c9346f8f7945e41a1b271a0310928ad10999bb2c","compact":"1595a176e53d1eda31df3ef2874911cd42373df39f0b4e9ee2a59895994666a0","nasal":"a93859fc27ab16067c072cabc1020262e85d366851b56b35b65b387835854e54"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-34-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":34,"verse":14,"english":"The king, versed in time and place, and pure, speedily summoning his treasurer, said to him these words firmly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-39-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2034014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6f58713a9e6fdee9f33230c385ebee63a96575ddd6b4f789a96983e01f932dfc","compact":"ff01aa54985fc6ab13fe1d137428eb4ee0c2d4b6baa0cc1feaf88dc6cbbff35f","nasal":"ff01aa54985fc6ab13fe1d137428eb4ee0c2d4b6baa0cc1feaf88dc6cbbff35f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-34-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":34,"verse":15,"english":"Do you without delay bring to Vaidehī excellent and costly attires and noble ornaments, counting these (ten and four) years.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.603,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-39-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2034015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"952f4a6ad952b7dba828008b725c5ff4062016fa4a880ef761957d8cef74bf65","compact":"755e0b19dddaea80a33e887ae82fa7fd19e4f9460995008d3194cd2b9d88db04","nasal":"755e0b19dddaea80a33e887ae82fa7fd19e4f9460995008d3194cd2b9d88db04"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-34-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":34,"verse":16,"english":"Thus desired by the foremost of men, that officer repairing to the treasury, procuring all those, speedily presented them to Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-39-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2034016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7756336f5133afc794a068adc86eb6e1b56db128bcb35cfd5d6b6b0b3b54eb99","compact":"a73c35ecd2bb614a9027891c1c930e0a6d86fa23dae46ac33887843d62b1ecd7","nasal":"b5636ae23a87a21a287e3f2e2d2d3b83b4e82416a444f80710ebb0d45e47794d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-34-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":34,"verse":17,"english":"Thereupon that pure-sprung one, Vaidehi, ordered to the forest, adorned her goodly limbs with those rare ornaments.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-39-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2034017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"78791788f898893d45405da0c416700e7f71656994a8ef4c373ddb651066efed","compact":"778501ae29a798c87df8e459a1db3ab105d5bcafa2ccf277b899e